From 42765381be0104ae2bce596678ba30197fc75ca4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gambot <56745325+GbotHQ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:08:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] gui: fix the recent-projects list - crash, leak, hang and
 the file you just opened

Four separate defects in the code path added with the UI-scaling work:

  * Clicking "Reset recent files list" crashed the application. The handler did
    `qobject_cast<MainMenuBar*>(this->parent())` and called it unconditionally, but this
    dialog is also constructed from the two FFmpeg checks in MainWindow, where the parent is
    the window - so the cast is null and onRecentsUpdate() wrote through a null this. That
    path is reachable: export with a missing or broken FFmpeg, and the modal settings dialog
    opens on the FFmpeg tab with the QoL tab one click away.

  * Every rebuild leaked eight QActions. The path actions were created with no parent, then
    removed from the menu and dropped from the `actions` vector, leaving them unreachable and
    unowned. Parenting them to the menu makes the clear() above delete them, and the loop that
    tried to tidy up is deleted: openRecent->disconnect(action) removes the *menu's* outgoing
    connections, of which there are none.

  * A stored recents list longer than eight entries hung the application at startup. The
    padding loop only ever appended, so `while (length != 8)` never terminated from above.

  * The project you had just opened never appeared in the list when the list was already full:
    the writer popped the oldest entry and never appended the new one, and the `contains`
    guard that followed meant an already-listed file never moved to the front. It is now
    prepend-and-cap, i.e. a most-recent-first list of eight.
---
 src/ctrl/System.cpp              | 24 ++++++++++----------
 src/gui/GeneralSettingDialog.cpp |  9 ++++++--
 src/gui/MainMenuBar.cpp          | 38 +++++++++++++++++---------------
 3 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ctrl/System.cpp b/src/ctrl/System.cpp
index cba74d1..4eb2159 100644
--- a/src/ctrl/System.cpp
+++ b/src/ctrl/System.cpp
@@ -124,19 +124,19 @@ System::openProject(const QString& aFileName, Project::Hook* aHookGrabbed, util:
             QSettings settings;
             QStringList recentfiles = settings.value("projectloader/recents").toStringList();
 
-            // Check file length
-            if (recentfiles.length() != 8) {
-                recentfiles.append(aFileName);
-            }
-            // If length eight remove first
-            else if (recentfiles.length() >= 8) {
-                recentfiles.pop_front();
-            }
-            // Save
-            if (!settings.value("projectloader/recents").toStringList().contains(aFileName)) {
-                settings.setValue("projectloader/recents", recentfiles);
-                settings.sync();
+            // Most-recent-first, capped at eight: record the file that was just opened and
+            // drop the oldest when full. The old branches did the opposite when the list was
+            // already full - they popped the oldest entry and never appended the new one - so
+            // the project you had just opened was missing from the menu that this same
+            // function refreshes a few lines below. The `contains` guard also prevented the
+            // list from ever being reordered, so it goes with it.
+            recentfiles.removeAll(aFileName);
+            recentfiles.prepend(aFileName);
+            while (recentfiles.length() > 8) {
+                recentfiles.pop_back();
             }
+            settings.setValue("projectloader/recents", recentfiles);
+            settings.sync();
             if (mainMenu != nullptr) {
                 mainMenu->onRecentsUpdate();
             }
